A||||9||burdell1||Windshield Wiper Burnout||||||
Z||000000||burdell1||08-21-99||01:47 PM||||I've had problems with my windshield wipers burning out fuses, (and circuit boards) before and now my windshield wipers are on all the time when they are in the "off" mode. I've found that whenever I put in a new circuit board in the motor, the wiper switch wires get really hot, and eventually part of the circuit board literally burns out, and then they are on all the time (I take out the fuse and put it back in when it's raining which is a pain) I figure that I need to replace the wiper switch, but that is a pain in the butt. Do you think that maybe there is a bad ground in the switch and that I could just cut the ground wire and wire it to the chassis? if so, do you know which one is the ground wire?  I have an 85 GT with intermittant wipers and cruise control.
Z||000001||Phil||08-21-99||03:05 PM||||I had a somewhat similar experience with my 85 GT the wipers would not stop when I hit mist. I'm in the midst of making a kitcar out of it so I haven't really checked to see if they run all the time. but while trying to make my windshield wiper linkage I would hit the mist button and they would not shut off until I turned off the key. Finally traced it down to sticky contact points in the wiper motor. I took off the plate and filed the contacts and all was well. 
Z||000002||burdell1||08-23-99||09:38 AM||||Does anybody know which one is the ground wire on the wiper switch?
Z||000003||theogre||08-23-99||11:39 AM||||buring things up usuallly means that the motor is drawing more current than it should. that or a short, but your not poping fuses......<p>some s10's use the same motor acording to one post I saw someplace.
Z||000004||burdell1||08-23-99||02:12 PM||||actually, I am popping fuses, sometimes. My roommate wired my circuit board with wire connecting it where the burn was on the circuit board. When I put this in, for a long time it worked fine. However, recently while trying different circuit boards (to see if I could find one that would make my wipers go faster since they are relatively slow) it would pop fueses whenever I had the wipers in the off mode.
Z||000005||theogre||08-23-99||02:20 PM||||could be a short, the motor, or the delay control box up under the dash. The stalk switch usually either works or it doesn't. The onlly thing I can think of that makes the motor draw when the control is off is when it's trying to "park". Parking cutoff is controlled by the switch in the wiper motor.
Z||000006||burdell1||08-23-99||04:20 PM||||Where is the control box under the dash? what is it next to?<br>
Z||000007||burdell1||12-19-1999||05:27 PM||||My car's wiper's are really slow as well....any idea what the cause is? also, is replacing the wiper switch hard to do yourself? Does anyone out there have one for an 85 GT with delay and cruise control?||||reg||5
Z||000008||theogre||12-20-1999||06:53 PM||||pull the motor off and go thru it. pull off the screens and check the wiper transmission( all the linkages and pivots, including the wiper arm shafts.) It sounds like the linkage or motor is binding or shorting in the motor. I don't think any of the controls will cause this unless they are really screwed up.<P>According to what i've read the wiper delay box is under the dash. no I don't know where. take the trim off below the stearing column for more room to look. Also according to what I've read you can take the connectors off the delay and plug them to eachother to bypass the delay box.||||reg||1
Z||000009||HF6582||12-20-1999||07:04 PM||||The delay box is behind the carpet straight down from the radio pod and on the other side is your subwoofer amp. Its a real pain in the A** to get to.<P>Scott||||reg||1
